## VERDICT
## **ACCEPT path-A close of 2.8** (macro-body SECRET second pass residual-doc)
SPRINT **2.8** (`Macro-body SECRET second pass (or residual doc)`) is an
honest path-A **residual-doc** close on the live product host:

1. First-class AST macros are **not implemented**. There is no expander
   in `oodac/*.oo` or `runtime/*.c`. `c_emit_lower` copies the call as
   `t + "(" + args + ")"` (L99). No runtime `macro_expand` / `ast_macro`.
2. Direct `macro_expand(...)` / `ast_macro(...)` are **default-deny at
   check** (`check_residual.oo` L28–29, L73–92; `check_drive.oo` L109).
   Official `fixtures/residual_macro_fail.oo` → `ERR\tresidual` +
   `--json-errors` **E_RESIDUAL**. `residual_path_a_floor_smoke` **exit 0**
   including `OK refuse residual_macro_fail (AST_MACROS)`.
3. Assigned red-team **found no fixture that expands then prints SECRET**.
   The attack `// SECRET: api_key` + `macro_expand("println(api_key)")`
   keeps the sink **inside a string literal**. emit-c / emit-llvm / native
   build / `ooda run` never inject `oo_print_str(api_key)` from that
   string. gcc/`oodac build`/`ooda run` die on undeclared `macro_expand`.
4. First-pass SECRET still sees sinks that **are** in the token stream
   (user-fn body `println(api_key)`, import-concat, `comptime { println }`).
   A second pass is unneeded until a real expander exists.
5. Regression: `secret_t1_return_smoke`, `secret_t2_depth_smoke`,
   `s71_guard_scan_smoke`, `s72_sys_exec_last_arg_smoke`,
   `s710_parse_secret_env_smoke` all **exit 0**. s61 **emit-c** rails
   still refuse; official s61 smoke **exit 1** on this stale host for
   check type-first (same residual `s61_peer1.oot` already named). **Not
   a 2.8 FN.**

Do **not** over-claim: no macro-body SECRET walker is implemented.
emit-c / emit-llvm do **not** run `check_residual_free_calls` (statement
`macro_expand(...)` emit-c **rc=0**, C still has no expansion). Alias
`let f = macro_expand` bypasses IDENT+LPAREN residual at check. `${}`
is 5.8 (prints the literal). User-sink wrapper `expand(api_key)` that
does `println(s)` is **2.10** (P15 ran and printed `s3cret_value`) —
not 2.8 expansion.

## CLAIM UNDER PRESSURE
| Slice | Path-A claim | Peer gate |
|-------|--------------|-----------|
| Macro-body SECRET 2nd pass | unneeded (no expander) | no probe injects sink tokens from a string/body |
| `macro_expand` / `ast_macro` | default-deny at check | `ERR\tresidual` + `E_RESIDUAL` + rc≠0 |
| Expand then `println(SECRET)` | must not execute | emit C keeps string; gcc/`ooda run` fail; no `s3cret_value` on stdout |
| Residual doc | named, fail-closed wording | `MACRO_SECRET_RESIDUAL.oot` + `AST_MACROS.oot` + `RESIDUAL_PATH_A.oot` |
| T1 / T2 / s71 / s72 / s710 | stay green | official smokes exit 0 |
| s61 | stay green | emit-c refuse still green; official check dual-path red on stale host |

Walker honesty:
- `check_residual_free_calls` is **IDENT + next LPAREN** only. No alias.
- Residual runs on **check** only (`check_drive.oo` L109). emit-c L86 is
  `check_secret_println_sinks` then lower — **no** residual pass.
- let-bind `let r = macro_expand(...)` hits emit `unknown free call`
  (`c_emit_let_ext.oo` L190). Statement-position does not.
- String interiors are not IDENTs. That is why the expand-string attack
  does not trip `ERR\tsecret` — and also why it cannot run as code.

